ign}\n\t\t\\big(\\hat{S}_{[\\mathrm{eval}_u(\\cdot_W) = a]}\n\t\t\\big)_{\\mathsf{A}\\mathsf{A}'}\n\t\t&\\simeq_{\\delta_S}\n\t\t\\big(\\hat{M}^{(\\mathrm{Point},W),u}_{a}\n\t\t\\big)_{\\mathsf{B}\\mathsf{A}''}\\,,\n\t\t\\label{eq:qld-s-point-con-alice} \\\\\n\t\t\\big(\\hat{S}_{[\\mathrm{eval}_u(\\cdot_W) = a]}\n\t\t\\big)_{\\mathsf{B}\\mathsf{B}'}\n\t\t&\\simeq_{\\delta_S}\n\t\t\\big(\\hat{M}^{(\\mathrm{Point},W),u}_{a}\n\t\t\\big)_{\\mathsf{A}\\mathsf{B}''}\\,,\n\t\t\\label{eq:qld-s-point-con-bob}\n\t\\end{align}\n\twhere $\\mathrm{eval}_u(\\cdot_W)$ denotes the evaluation at the point $u$\n\tof the first outcome $g_X$ if $W = X$, and of the second outcome $g_Z$\n\tif $W = Z$.\n\\end{lemma}\n\\begin{proof}\n\t\\uses{lem:qld-4-13-established, lem:qld-4-12, thm:naimark,\n\t\tlem:ld-soundness, def:ld-game, fact:agreement, fact:add-a-proj2,\n\t\tfact:data-processing, lem:schwartz-zippel-total-degree,\n\t\tdef:combine-map}\n\tLemma~\\ref{lem:qld-4-13-established} supplies measurements on the directly\n\tindexed line carrier: an axis line records its base point and directly sampled\n\tcoordinate index, while a diagonal line also records a direction whose earlier\n\tcoordinates vanish. Its averages use the corresponding\n\tdirectly indexed line-point law, and its consistency relations use the completed\n\tanswer alphabet $\\F_q \\cup \\{\\bot\\}$. These data are not yet a strategy for the\n\tclassical low individual degree game of Definition~\\ref{def:ld-game}, whose line\n\tquestions retain a field-valued seed. Such a strategy requires a transport from\n\tthe directly indexed carrier and law to the seed-indexed question distribution,\n\tand a conversion from the completed-answer relations, including degenerate\n\tzero-direction lines, to the game's field-valued answer checks. These open\n\ttransports are recorded in \\cite{gap:qpbt_ld-dimension-divisibility} and\n\t\\cite{gap:qpbt_combined-lines-error-term}.\n\tConditional on these transports, Lemmas~\\ref{lem:qld-4-12}\n\tand~\\ref{lem:qld-4-13-established} give a strategy with parameters\n\t$(q,2m+2,d,1)$ and success probability $1-\\delta_{\\mathrm{combine}}$; the\n\taxis-parallel clause supplies the required degree-$d$ answer format. The\n\tnumerical estimate available for $\\delta_{\\mathrm{combine}}$ is\n\t$C \\cdot m \\cdot \\poly(\\eps,md/q)$, not the unproved form\n\t$\\poly(m^2\\eps,md/q)$ printed in Lemma~\\ref{lem:qld-4-13}\n\t(Remark~\\ref{rem:qld-4-13-source-defects}). The error function $\\delta_S$\n\tabsorbs the prefactor $m$ into $(md)^a$.\n\t(For $(q, 2m+2, d, 1)$ to be a parameter tuple of\n\tDefinition~\\ref{def:ld-game} the dimension $2m+2$ must divide $q$;\n\tadmissibility of $(q,m,d)$ supplies only that $m$ divides $q$, and for\n\tadmissible parameters with $m \\ge 2$ the divisibility fails, so this\n\tinstantiation is an unresolved obligation of the source argument,\n\trecorded in Remark~\\ref{rem:qld-4-7-divisibility} and analyzed in\n\t\\cite{gap:qpbt_ld-dimension-divisibility}.) Since $\\{\\hat{Q}^{\\ell}_{f}\\}$ is\n\tonly a POVM, it is first made projective by Naimark dilation\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
